        <Anchor elementId="RXN-7984_anchor" position="0.5" shapeType="Circle" />
      </Waypoints>
      <Graphics lineColor="000000" lineStyle="Solid" lineWidth="1.0" connectorType="Straight" />
      <Comment source="BioCyc">Along with EC 1.14.13.90, zeaxanthin epoxidase, this enzyme forms part of the xanthophyll (or violaxanthin) cycle for controlling the concentration of zeaxanthin in chloroplasts. It is activated by a low pH of the thylakoid lumen (produced by high light intensity). Zeaxanthin induces the dissipation of excitation energy in the chlorophyll of the light-harvesting protein complex of photosystem II. In higher plants the enzyme reacts with all-trans-diepoxides, such as violaxanthin, and all-trans-monoepoxides, but in the alga Mantoniella squamata, only the diepoxides are good substrates.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="RXN-7984" />
      <Property key="Orphan" value=":NO" />
      <Property key="Pathways" value="RXN-13185, PWY-5945" />
      <Property key="PathwayCount" value="2" />
